# env.example — copy to .env ONLY if a connection uses a token instead of signing in.
#
# Most connections in ../ sign in with OAuth and need nothing here.
# Never commit .env. Never put a .env in a shared drive: everyone with access to
# the folder could read it. In a shared drive, each person connects through their
# own account in their own app instead.
#
# Placeholders only. Variable names must match what the server's own
# documentation asks for — check it, then rename these if they differ.

# Atlassian — only where an organisation admin has enabled API tokens
# (Jira Service Management requires one).
# ATLASSIAN_SITE=<your-site>.atlassian.net
# ATLASSIAN_EMAIL=<you@example.com>
# ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN=<token created in your Atlassian account settings>
